{
  "about": "EVM nodes as templates the brain enforces for each relay vault (contracts/brain/src/evm.rs; set with x {\"evm_template\": {\"template\": ...}}). The brain builds each call, the vault signs it: fixed arguments are fixed here, 'vault' is the vault's own address, the keeper only fills at_most amounts (capped) and floor minimums (never below amount x num / den); a 'market' minimum is also never below the oracle's price for the amount less slippage_bps (the brain reads the two feeds, named as in the vault's oracle_setup: eth, usdc, nvda; each confirmed by its backup; no fresh price, no signature), a 'share' minimum is a market minimum where one side is an LP share priced from its two tokens' feeds and the k the owner pins (see shares below), and a 'deadline' is block time + 5 minutes, whatever the keeper sends. The feed name 'usd' is exactly one dollar, never read (USDG, which no oracle prices). Every swap and zap here has a market or share minimum (a fixed floor alone, ~90% of the market, is room to sandwich): Base WETH -> USDC (1%), the Robinhood v4 swaps (3%: the ETH/NVDA pool's 1% fee and its gap to the feeds, ~1% on 2026-11-09), the ETHNVDA pair token zap and redeem (3%: the same pool, and it is thin, ~$5.5k at full range) and Smart LP deposit and withdraw (1%: a 0.3% pool and 10 bps retention). The fixed floors stay as the owner's backstop. NVDA's feed is Chainlink RHNVDA/USD on Robinhood Chain, its backup the 30-min TWAP of the NVDA/USDG 0.05% Uniswap v3 pool there (scripts/keeper/src/twap.ts); when the stock market is closed Chainlink pauses and nothing in NVDA trades. Fixed floors were set on 2026-11-06 (Base: 1 WETH ~ 2,224 USDC; Robinhood: 0.01 ETH ~ 0.1186 NVDA, 0.05 NVDA ~ 0.0041 ETH, 0.01 ETH ~ 0.01707 ETHNVDA shares, owner floor ~90% of that), the Smart LP ones on 2026-11-09 (50 USDG ~ 5.59e6 share-wei of sdAMZN-FR-USDG, owner floor ~89%): owners set their own. Tested on forks: contracts/sandbox/tests/evm_fork.rs (Base), evm_fork_robinhood.rs and ladder_fork_robinhood.rs (Robinhood Chain).",
