      "shares": {
        "about": "How a 'share' leaf prices an LP share (contracts/brain/src/oracle.rs ShareValue): USD per whole share = k x sqrt(P_a x P_b) / 1e18, P_a and P_b the two tokens' feeds (USD, 1e18). A full-range position of liquidity L is worth 2 L sqrt(P_a P_b) at the FEEDS' prices whatever the pool's price is (which a sandwich moves), so per share k = 1e18 x 2 L / S, decimals folded in. The owner pins k in the template from the chain; the keeper gives no number to it (no price, no L, no S). L / S only grows (fees compounded in, withdrawal fees left behind), so a pinned k is at most the true one: a redeem's floor from it is never above fair, a deposit's asks for at least fair less slippage, and once the share has grown past the slippage it refuses and the owner pins a fresh k.",
        "ETHNVDA": "k = 1e18 x 2 x positionLiquidity() / totalSupply() (both tokens 18 decimals): 2,006,968,196,877,436,792 on 2026-11-09 (L 4,460,122,564,624,555,222, S 4,444,637,011,751,242,718; $1,231.83 a share at ETH $2,104.32, NVDA $179.02).",
        "sdAMZN-FR-USDG": "k = 1e18 x (totalValueQuote() / 1e6) / (totalSupply() / 1e18) / sqrt(P_amzn) (USDG is 'usd'): 551,882,584,226,203,459,448,670,186,493 on 2026-11-09 (8,923 USDG units over 1,000 share-wei, AMZN $261.41). totalValueQuote is the vault's own 30-min TWAP valuation; within 0.1% of Chainlink's that day."
      }
    }
